"Andrew Stone" <nospam@nospam.com> writes:
> Are there limits to where a cursed scroll of teleport can take you?
>
> The reason I ask is, I was just fighting Vlad in the top level of his
> tower, and he read a scroll of teleport.
> 
> I am assuming it was cursed, because he disappeared from the level.

Alternatively, he could have been confused.

> His tower entrance was on level 37 - is there some level range where
> this scroll will take you if you don't have teleport control?

In general, a cursed or confused scroll has a 20% chance of leaving a
monster where it is (100% in the Endgame, Fort Ludios, or if carrying
the Amulet); otherwise, it takes a monster to a random level between
DL 1 and three deeper than the current level, other than the current
level. It won't take it downwards further than the bottom of the
branch it's in, or outside the bounds of the Quest, or to the Sanctum
level before the invocation has been performed.

